hi i'm kanchan khoya the founder of  spice spice baby and i love curry it's  dreamy it's creamy it's packed with  spices you can put whatever you want in  it and i think anyone should be able to  have curry anytime they want so today  i'm going to be showing you how to make  a three minute curry a 30 minute curry  and a three hour curry so let's get  started  say you only have three minutes but you  really want curry with as much of the  flavor as possible this recipe is for  you it's probably going to offend some  curry aficionados but we're going to be  okay with that in the name of efficiency  first we're going to create our curry  sauce by using coconut cream one of the  things i love about curry is the creamy  texture which is kind of challenging to  achieve in three minutes so the coconut  cream instead of coconut milk really  helps us do that we're gonna add onion  powder garlic powder and ginger powder  one of the things i love about curry is  that you get to layer aromatics like  onion garlic and ginger and oil but  since we only have three minutes we're  just gonna hack that by adding the  powders instead then we're gonna add  cayenne for heat then we add some  turmeric garam masala for those smoky  notes cumin and coriander powder now  we're going to add salt to taste  and some black pepper  mix this all together  sure is easier than cooking a curry on  the stove for hours finally we're gonna  add our canned chickpeas that have been  well rinsed and drained and now we're  just gonna cover this now we're gonna  put this in the microwave for three  minutes until it's hot and all those  amazing flavors have had some time to  get to know each other curry in a hurry  that smells really good so now we're  just gonna take off the cling wrap and  marvel at the fact that we just made  curry in three minutes we're just gonna  stir in some chopped spinach so it's  gonna wilt down quicker a hit of lime  juice for those citrusy flavor notes and  then we're just gonna mix this all  together  my mom would be really impressed with  this hack it truly smells like the real  deal i'm not even gonna lie we're gonna  spoon it onto some steamed rice we're  gonna hit it with some fresh cilantro  for vibrancy and we're gonna taste it  this is shockingly delicious i can taste  the citrus all the spices the different  notes the creaminess from the coconut  for three minutes this tastes like a  legit curry this is great for busy  weeknights when you want to make  something your kids are going to lap up  even if your indian mother-in-law would  not approve say you want something a bit  more authentic and you have a little bit  more time this next 30-minute recipe is  just for you  while most people are familiar with  north indian curry recipes this  particular one is inspired by southern  india and while i'm technically north  indian i have to say this is one of my  favorites we're going to start by  warming our coconut oil on medium heat  to which we're going to add our mustard  seeds and we're going to allow these to  sizzle and even splatter a little bit  it's going to wake up the spices and add  so much flavor and now we're going to  toss in our curry leaves just as those  curry leaves are starting to crisp up  about 30 seconds or so we're gonna add  our green chilies the green chili is  gonna add spice it's totally optional  but come on and then we're gonna add our  sliced onions and give that all a nice  toss smells so good  this combination of mustard seeds curry  leaves and oil can be drizzled on your  favorite salad on soups and really on  anything it is a classic base for most  southern indian dishes i'm going to let  these onions cook down until soft for  about five minutes  now that my onions have softened i'm  gonna add a tablespoon of minced ginger  and four cloves of minced garlic and  just allow that to cook until fragrant  you definitely don't want to burn it  once you can smell that ginger and  garlic and it smells so good we're going  to add in two teaspoons of tandoori  masala so i am cheating a little with  the tandoori spice blend because this is  a 30 minute weeknight friendly curry  once you can start to smell that spice  blend it's time to add the tomatoes the  tomatoes are not just going to add a  sauce but they're also gonna give us  these beautiful tangy notes at this  point we're gonna let this cook for  about three minutes and while these are  cooking you may be wondering how can  this be a curry when it doesn't have  curry powder let's talk about that we  don't really have a thing called curry  powder curry is such a broad concept in  india it really varies from family to  family region to region and that's why  i'm not adding just straight curry  powder to this but it's still very much  a curry now that our spiced curry base  is done we're going to add some chopped  chicken you can do any kind of protein  like fish or you could also go  completely plant-based and do chickpeas  again we're going to hit this with salt  pepper  i'm just gonna toss this chicken to get  it well coated with the spice mixture  and until it's no longer pink and then  we're gonna add the coconut milk some  tamarind paste  and sugar this is looking creamy i can  smell the tamarind and the aroma and the  smoky notes from that spice blend this  is going to be good we're just going to  cover this on medium heat and let it  cook for about 15 minutes until the  chicken is cooked through it's been 15  minutes and i am just transported back  to my childhood i can smell those spices  and the coconut and i just want to dive  in we're just gonna spoon this over  plain steamed rice we're gonna hit it  with fresh cilantro again because that's  just what we do and because i like heat  i'm gonna do a little sprinkling of  chili powder totally optional unless  you're me  a little bit more people think curry is  so complicated but it's really just  about layering flavor adding a little  bit of this a little bit of that and  this is the result i cannot wait to try  it  don't burn your mouth  oh  that is so good like a hug in a bowl  comfort food at its best we have the  sweetness from the little bit of sugar  we have the tang from the tomatoes and  the tamarind we have all those smoky  notes from the spices a little bit of  heat it is really a party in the mouth  so i've shown you two pretty quick and  straightforward curry recipes but say  you want to really up your game impress  your guests this next recipe is gonna  blow their minds  while our 30-minute recipe took  inspiration from the southern part of  india today we're gonna be making rogan  josh a traditional kashmiri meat curry  here we have some cubed beef to which  we're gonna add garam masala spice blend  and sea salt give it a good toss to coat  the meat with the spices garam masala is  very often used in many indian dishes  particularly in northern indian curries  it has smoky notes from clove cinnamon  cardamom bay leaf black pepper and a  host of other really mesmerizing spices  and it goes so well with any meat dish  now we're going to brown the beef in  batches without overcrowding the pan  until it is nice and brown on all sides  coating the beef in the garam masala  really allows us to get that layering of  flavor now that my beef is nice and  brown i'm going to take it out on a  sheet pan where it can rest don't  discard anything from the pan it has all  the flavor and all the juices from the  beef and now we're going to use that to  saute our onions i'm going to add a  little salt to the onions to season as i  go and to help them soften a little bit  quicker i'm just gonna saute these  onions until they're soft for about five  minutes some people like to really get  the onions nice and golden brown do  whatever feels right for you it's all a  personal preference our onion is nice  and softened even a little brown to that  we're gonna add our ginger and garlic  you can start to see that a lot of  curries have this kind of onion ginger  garlic in oil base in common now that  the ginger and garlic is nice and  fragrant i'm going to add my whole  spices i'm adding black peppercorns  green and black cardamom some whole  cloves  a cinnamon stick dried red chilies and  bay leaves we're going to saute these  whole spices with the onion ginger  garlic mixture for just about a minute  until nice and toasted and fragrant and  then we're going to add our turmeric red  pepper  cumin coriander  fennel powder and some dry fenugreek  leaves sauteing the spices at the  beginning of the curry as a base here is  really activating the flavor a lot of  the volatile compounds and just waking  up those spices so unlike the earlier  dish where we use the pre-existing  tandoori blend here we're really  building our own rogan josh spice blend  our spices are toasted and beautifully  aromatic and now we're going to add back  our browned beef so because spices have  antibacterial properties they were used  back in the day to prevent meat from  spoiling almost like a pre-refrigeration  refrigeration hack so we're getting the  beef all nice and coated with the spice  mixture and then to this we are going to  add some whipped yogurt some people now  actually add tomato to rogan josh for  tang we're going with greek yogurt  now that the beef is nicely coated with  that spiced yogurt mixture we're just  gonna add enough water to cover  salt and pepper  now we're just gonna let this cook low  and slow for two and a half hours until  that beef is nice and tender and all the  flavors have merged beautifully together  now that our rogan josh is simmering  away we're gonna make roti roti or  indian flatbread is a staple in every  house while it can seem intimidating you  and me were in this together and we're  gonna figure it out so first we're gonna  add whole wheat flour half a cup of warm  water a little bit of oil  and some salt so i'm just gonna toss  everything together and then i'm going  in with my hands so you wanna knead this  until the dough comes together  and does not stick to your fingers if  your dough is a little sticky just add a  little bit more flour my dough has now  come together i'm just going to let this  rest for 30 minutes under this damp  towel and we'll be back now that our  dough has rested it's time to roll out  the roti so we're just going to take a  little piece with our hands you don't  have to be super precise here you're  going to make a little ball  and then sprinkle your surface with  flour so it doesn't stick coat my little  circle with flowers so it's easier to  roll and then we roll roll a little bit  turn a little bit  roll  turn  roll turn that should get you to a  perfect circle if your dinner guests  judge you for your roti not being a  perfect circle  i think you should send them home this  is a great activity to get your kids  involved in sensory skill building  resilience building because it's not  gonna be a circle they're gonna have to  be okay with failure this looks great so  i'm gonna set this guy aside and roll  out the rest now it's time to cook the  rotis the trick here is to get the pan  scorching hot almost to the point where  it's uncomfortable to place your hand  right above it we're gonna place the  rotis in the hot dry skillet for about  two minutes you want your roti to puff  up but if it doesn't don't worry about  it it's gonna taste just as good so i'm  just gonna flip it i'm gonna let this go  for another 30 seconds to a minute okay  and then we're just going to top it with  a little bit of butter  for extra moisture and deliciousness  that's our first roti i'm going to cook  up the rest and once that's done we're  going to be ready to bring our roti and  curry together  so our roti is done our rogan josh is  done let's bring it all together i'm  totally plating a whole red chili  because i will eat it as always a little  garnish of cilantro so i'm just gonna go  right in using the roti almost as a  spoon to pick up my succulent beef rogan  josh  i can taste those rich and warm spices  the succulent beef the tangy yogurt the  roti is just perfect to soak up all  those flavors this is the ultimate  comfort food three hours may seem like a  lot of time to make a dish but trust me  this rogan josh is worth it so there you  have it three curries in three different  amounts of time we have the three-minute  microwave curry for when you want curry  in a hurry we have a 30-minute curry for  when you want a really delicious meal on  a week night and then we have a  three-hour curry for when you really  want to impress someone special i hope  you make them all and let me know which  one is your favorite in the comments  below i'm kanchan and there's always  time for curry oh yes  [Music]  [Music]  you

